emain hungry, i.e. without cheese.\n\n## Input\n\nThe first line of the input contains four integer numbers N ( 1ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë N ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë10 5 ), M ( 0ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë M ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë10 5 ), Y 0 ( 0ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë Y 0 ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë10 7 ), Y 1 ( 0ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë Y 1 ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë10 7 , Y 0 ΓÇëΓëáΓÇë Y 1 ). The second line contains a strictly increasing sequence of N numbers ΓÇö x coordinates of mice. Third line contains a strictly increasing sequence of M numbers ΓÇö x coordinates of cheese. All coordinates are integers and do not exceed 10 7 by absolute value.\n\n## Output\n\nThe only line of output should contain one number ΓÇö the minimal number of mice which will remain without cheese.\n\n## Examples\n\nExample 1:\n```\n3 2 0 2\n0 1 3\n2 5\n```\n```\n1\n```\n\n## Note\n\nAll the three mice will choose the first piece of cheese. Second and third mice will eat this piece. The first one will remain hungry, because it was running towards the same piece, but it was late. The second piece of cheese will remain uneaten.","type":"text"}],"contestId":76,"index":"B","memoryLimit":"256 megabytes","name":"Mice","problemKey":"76-B","rating":null,"tags":[],"timeLimit":"0.5 second","url":"https://codeforces.com/contest/76/problem/B"},{"approaches":[{"label":"Approach 1","number":1,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 2","number":2,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 3","number":3,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 4","number":4,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 5","number":5,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 6","number":6,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 7","number":7,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 8","number":8,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","langu